WEBVTT

00:00:21.245 --> 00:00:22.872
Who likes good news?

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:25.750
Everyone? Then, good news, everyone.

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:29.503
Our next delivery isn't to
some dangerous outer space planet.

00:00:29.587 --> 00:00:30.630
It's to Earth.

00:00:30.755 --> 00:00:33.758
Earth is dangerous.
I fell off my chair there once.

00:00:33.841 --> 00:00:34.884
Ow!

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:36.135
Quit it, Earth.

00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:38.638
We won't even have to leave
New New York.

00:00:38.721 --> 00:00:41.140
The package is going to Long Long Island.

00:00:41.223 --> 00:00:45.478
Yes, to the lavish Mafia-style villa
of the Donbot.

00:00:45.561 --> 00:00:48.481
The Donbot? The vicious Robot Gangster?

00:00:48.564 --> 00:00:52.193
I'd better use my special robot vision
to see what's inside.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.364
It looks like a pair of clamps.

00:00:59.408 --> 00:01:01.494
When are those new clamps
going to get here?

00:01:01.577 --> 00:01:03.871
These are all rusted out
with snitch juice.

00:01:03.955 --> 00:01:07.083
Patience, Clamps,
it is my eldest daughter's wedding day.

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:10.086
You don't want the Space Pope
to see you clamping, now, do you?

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.713
Oh, geez, I forgot my Pope manners.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.181
Dearly beloved,

00:01:22.264 --> 00:01:25.685
it is with the great speed that I now
pronounce you husband and wife.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.025
-Hey!
-What the...

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:39.073
May I help you with some assistance?

00:01:39.156 --> 00:01:42.535
Delivery for Francis X. Clampazzo?

00:01:42.618 --> 00:01:44.620
We don't got nobody here by that alias.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.998
Hey, hey, that's me.
Are those my new clamps?

00:01:47.081 --> 00:01:48.541
Your name's Francis?

00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:50.126
Oh!

00:01:51.627 --> 00:01:56.340
Guys, look, it's Calculon,
and the Robot Devil, and an open bar.

00:01:56.424 --> 00:01:57.925
What's not to sneak into?

00:01:58.676 --> 00:02:01.304
Bender, you can't crash a mob wedding.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:05.891
You forget, Leela.
I'm Bender, owner of disguise.

00:02:05.975 --> 00:02:10.396
And now, ladies and gentlemen,
my good friend, Calculon.

00:02:11.606 --> 00:02:14.066
Hey, this one's for the new couple.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.361
It's your day. It's all about you.

00:02:17.862 --> 00:02:20.740
Who's that singing at your wedding?

00:02:20.823 --> 00:02:25.411
It's Calculon, Calculon, Calculon

00:02:27.204 --> 00:02:31.500
Hey. Oh. Piscopo. This guy.

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.676
Bada-boing.

00:02:42.011 --> 00:02:43.763
Hey, sexy, I'm Bender.

00:02:43.846 --> 00:02:46.182
What brings you to this tacky soirée?

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.726
-I'm the bride.
-Oops.

00:02:48.809 --> 00:02:51.062
How about you, baby? Want to do it?

00:02:51.145 --> 00:02:53.773
-Bender, it's me, Fanny.
-You who?

00:02:53.856 --> 00:02:55.399
The Donbot's wife?

00:02:55.816 --> 00:02:57.360
We had an affair.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:00.196
An affair, huh? Sounds like me.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:02.031
Geez, I'd better be a little more careful.

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:04.825
I don't want to hit on anybody
I already had sex with.

00:03:08.704 --> 00:03:09.747
Hiya, Bella.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.082
Hi, Mom.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.167
What about you? You're my third choice.

00:03:26.681 --> 00:03:29.600
Oh, Bender,
this is all happening too slowly.

00:03:29.684 --> 00:03:30.851
Let's get married.

00:03:30.935 --> 00:03:32.853
Quiet, I'm making out with a floozy.

00:03:36.524 --> 00:03:38.567
Hold your clapper. Someone's coming.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:46.367
Donbot, please, I'll pay you back
as soon as you lend me some more money.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.829
Sorry, Calculon.
It gives me no joy to do this,

00:03:49.912 --> 00:03:51.414
because Clamps will be doing it.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.874
Clamps, here are your new clamps.

00:03:53.958 --> 00:03:55.126
Clamps!

00:03:58.629 --> 00:04:00.298
No, no.

00:04:00.881 --> 00:04:01.882
Line?

00:04:02.174 --> 00:04:06.053
No!

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:09.015
Yeah, Daddy hates welchers.

00:04:09.098 --> 00:04:11.392
The only thing he hates worse
is witnesses.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.729
And guys who mess around
with his daughters.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.025
And attempt to duplicate
his meatball recipe.

00:04:26.449 --> 00:04:27.658
How was the wedding, Bender?

00:04:27.825 --> 00:04:29.702
Says who? I didn't witness anything!

00:04:29.785 --> 00:04:33.789
In entertainment news,
two-time Oscar pool winner, Calculon,

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:37.293
was brutally clamped yesterday
by an unknown assailant.

00:04:37.418 --> 00:04:39.795
Poor Calculon.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.464
All right, Amy, you win!

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.590
The mob did it.

00:04:42.673 --> 00:04:46.594
I saw the whole thing while also having
hot sex with the Donbot's daughter.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:51.057
I'm scared and great at sex.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.892
Bender, you need to go to the police

00:04:52.975 --> 00:04:56.062
and tell them a tastefully edited version
of what you just said.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.689
What, and have the Mafia
come after me, too?

00:04:58.773 --> 00:05:02.193
No way. This secret goes to my grave.

00:05:02.276 --> 00:05:04.570
The Bureau is offering anyone
with information

00:05:04.654 --> 00:05:08.491
about this gangland-style clamping
a $50 reward.

00:05:08.616 --> 00:05:09.742
Ooh! Ooh!

00:05:09.825 --> 00:05:13.829
And then Calculon said, "No, no. No!"

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:16.290
And then I ate some excellent meatballs.

00:05:16.374 --> 00:05:17.959
Can I have my 50 bucks now?

00:05:18.042 --> 00:05:21.295
I enjoyed your story,
especially the tasteful love scene,

00:05:21.379 --> 00:05:23.631
but it's not enough to convict the Donbot.

00:05:23.714 --> 00:05:26.968
You'll have to testify in open court.

00:05:27.051 --> 00:05:28.678
No. No!

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.221
Can I have another $50?

00:05:30.304 --> 00:05:31.305
-No.
-No?

00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:33.849
-No!
-No!

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:41.941
All rise for the Honorable Judge 723.

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.110
Be seated.

00:05:44.193 --> 00:05:46.862
Organized crime
is a plague on our society,

00:05:46.988 --> 00:05:51.200
and I will not tolerate
any form of intimidation during...

00:05:52.994 --> 00:05:55.705
All rise for the Honorable Judge 724.

00:05:56.372 --> 00:05:59.166
Good day. I'd like to say
I'm prepared to tolerate several,

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.044
if not all forms of intimidation
during this trial.

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:03.212
Prosecutor?

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:06.549
Your Honor, the prosecution pecks
for a mistrial

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:08.551
on the grounds of jury tampering.

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:14.473
-Donbot?
-Motion denied.

00:06:14.557 --> 00:06:16.517
Prosecutor, call your first witness.

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:20.021
The People call our star witness, Mr. X,

00:06:20.104 --> 00:06:24.191
whose appearance will be altered
because he's in grave danger.

00:06:28.613 --> 00:06:30.990
Bender, I've been looking for you.

00:06:31.073 --> 00:06:33.367
Which cake do you like better
for our wedding?

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.660
Bender?

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:36.787
Fix it, fix it, fix it, fix it!

00:06:37.955 --> 00:06:39.540
Whew, that was close.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:44.003
Isn't it true, Mr. X, that you are
slandering this innocent Mafioso

00:06:44.086 --> 00:06:46.464
to distract from your own felonious past,

00:06:46.547 --> 00:06:51.344
including a crime you made up yourself
called "burgle-arson-arceny"?

00:06:51.427 --> 00:06:55.348
That's a wholly-owned trademark
of Rodriguez Crime Concepts, Inc.

00:06:55.431 --> 00:06:57.767
Besides, I'm not on trial here.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.394
That's true.
You're on trial in Courtroom Three.

00:07:02.271 --> 00:07:05.775
You are charged with two counts
of burgle-arson-arceny.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:06.901
How do you plead?

00:07:06.984 --> 00:07:08.569
Not inno-guilty-cent.

00:07:10.947 --> 00:07:13.699
And then the Donbot said,
"Sorry, Calculon,"

00:07:13.783 --> 00:07:17.161
and then Calculon said, "No!"

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.248
I think we've heard enough.

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:24.293
Wait, I'm not finished. "O!"
Now I'm finished.

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:27.380
Your Honor, the prosecution roosts.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.638
Have you reached a verdict?

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.056
Indeed.

00:07:37.139 --> 00:07:41.477
After a steamy 12-way deliberation,
we find the accused guilty as...

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.561
Wait.

00:07:42.645 --> 00:07:44.272
The Donbot is innocent.

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:48.609
Calculon, who is that escorting you?

00:07:48.693 --> 00:07:50.528
Yes, who?

00:07:50.611 --> 00:07:53.906
My personal trainer,
and he's trained me to say

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.950
that my wounds were self-inflicted,

00:07:56.033 --> 00:08:01.831
for, you see, I am a big, Hollywood idiot,
dumb guy what does that sort of thing.

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:03.207
Perfect.

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.545
We find the Donbot...

00:08:08.296 --> 00:08:09.630
Dramatic pause.

00:08:09.714 --> 00:08:11.090
Not guilty.

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:12.883
What?

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:19.223
Honey, if you're marrying Bender,

00:08:19.307 --> 00:08:21.892
you might want to get a black dress
for the wedding.

00:08:21.976 --> 00:08:23.519
That's going to look hot.

00:08:31.527 --> 00:08:32.653
Don't be scared, Bender.

00:08:32.737 --> 00:08:35.281
We're putting you
in the Witness Relocation Program.

00:08:35.364 --> 00:08:39.076
You'll be given a new identity,
a new place to live, and this iPod.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:40.328
I don't want it anymore.

00:08:40.411 --> 00:08:42.246
So I gotta hide forever?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.958
No, just until the Robot Mafia
finds and kills you.

00:08:46.042 --> 00:08:47.335
They're pretty good at that.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.339
Goodbye, Professor.

00:08:51.422 --> 00:08:56.385
Before I leave, I just want you to know
I've never done any work whatsoever.

00:08:57.011 --> 00:09:00.431
Zoidberg, I know it seems
like I can't stand you.

00:09:01.766 --> 00:09:05.186
Leela, you'll have to watch out
for Fry now.

00:09:05.269 --> 00:09:06.354
Oh, Lord.

00:09:07.063 --> 00:09:09.440
I wish I could go with you, pal.

00:09:09.523 --> 00:09:11.776
Me, too. I'll need a butler.

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:13.945
Bender, we have to go.

00:09:28.793 --> 00:09:31.295
There'll never be another like him.

00:09:31.379 --> 00:09:33.464
Let's hire someone better.

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:38.928
Clamps. Clamps!

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:40.096
Huh?

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:41.889
Listen to my boss words.

00:09:41.973 --> 00:09:45.059
I would like you
to apply for Bender's old job

00:09:45.142 --> 00:09:47.812
and cozy up to this Fry, his best friend.

00:09:47.937 --> 00:09:51.691
Yeah, and then I'll introduce him
to my best friend,

00:09:51.774 --> 00:09:53.359
clamp number one!

00:09:53.526 --> 00:09:54.610
Sorry, toots.

00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:56.696
No, Clamps. No clamps.

00:09:57.029 --> 00:10:02.618
Sooner or later, Bender will contact Fry
as relocated-squealers always do.

00:10:02.785 --> 00:10:05.413
Then with the clamps, Francis.

00:10:05.871 --> 00:10:08.249
Francis... Francis?

00:10:08.332 --> 00:10:10.418
I'll clamp you with the Francis!

00:10:10.501 --> 00:10:12.336
Hey, whoa! Take it ease.

00:10:14.672 --> 00:10:17.091
Hey there, slick, I'm here about the job.

00:10:17.174 --> 00:10:18.342
Take a seat.

00:10:18.592 --> 00:10:20.886
We'll begin the interview shortly.

00:10:24.974 --> 00:10:26.934
We'll start with Andrew.

00:10:27.435 --> 00:10:29.228
Yeah, they all kind of broke.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.731
So, when do I start?

00:10:31.897 --> 00:10:33.899
Everyone, this is Francis.

00:10:33.983 --> 00:10:35.359
-Hey, Francis.
-Hello, Francis.

00:10:35.443 --> 00:10:36.694
-Hello.
-Cute name.

00:10:36.777 --> 00:10:38.529
Look what he can do.

00:10:40.906 --> 00:10:42.325
-Wow!
-Whoa!

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:43.868
Yeah, I do it all.

00:10:43.951 --> 00:10:46.454
Clamping, crimping, occasional snipping.

00:10:46.537 --> 00:10:47.747
Snipping?

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:51.667
Looks like you
may be out of a job, Zoidberg.

00:10:51.792 --> 00:10:53.961
That's all good fun,

00:10:54.045 --> 00:10:58.090
but of course a clamp is no substitute
for the precision of a genuine...

00:10:58.174 --> 00:10:59.967
Francis, would you do the honors?

00:11:02.803 --> 00:11:04.305
Stay off my turf!

00:11:04.513 --> 00:11:08.059
Yeesh. That guy can bite
my shiny metal clamps.

00:11:08.142 --> 00:11:11.312
You remind me
of my old friend Bender.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.023
Oh, yeah? Where does he safely live?

00:11:14.106 --> 00:11:15.107
I don't know.

00:11:15.191 --> 00:11:17.151
Hey, you want to come to my house
and play?

00:11:17.276 --> 00:11:19.737
Yeah, sounds like freakin' fun.

00:11:46.889 --> 00:11:50.101
Four stinking years of clamping school
for this?

00:11:50.184 --> 00:11:52.019
Greetings, Francis.

00:11:52.103 --> 00:11:54.647
Sorry if I was a little hostile before,

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:58.651
but snipping is the only reason
I'm even tolerated around here.

00:11:58.734 --> 00:12:03.030
Not like you,
with those magnificent squeezers.

00:12:03.281 --> 00:12:05.700
Squeezers? Squeezers?

00:12:05.908 --> 00:12:07.118
They're clamps, you!

00:12:07.368 --> 00:12:09.787
And if I want to -ing
snip with these clamps,

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.290
I will snip with these -ing clamps!

00:12:12.373 --> 00:12:14.709
Why do you think they call me...

00:12:15.209 --> 00:12:16.585
Francis?

00:12:16.669 --> 00:12:19.463
Francis, I have good news!

00:12:19.547 --> 00:12:21.924
It's time for your first delivery.

00:12:22.008 --> 00:12:23.551
To the Moon!

00:12:23.801 --> 00:12:26.053
Fan--ing-tastic!

00:12:42.528 --> 00:12:45.197
Here's the 200 feet of rope you ordered,
Sheriff Furley.

00:12:45.281 --> 00:12:49.160
Hot diggity! You fellers want to
stick around for the hanging tomorrow?

00:12:49.243 --> 00:12:50.536
It's gonna be a doozy.

00:12:51.996 --> 00:12:54.582
I sure do love hanging people.

00:12:54.665 --> 00:12:56.959
Well, I best start cutting the nooses.

00:12:57.043 --> 00:12:58.878
Oh! You know who could help with that?

00:13:00.004 --> 00:13:01.881
Francis!

00:13:06.218 --> 00:13:08.220
Nice job, Francis.

00:13:08.304 --> 00:13:11.932
I like how you didn't get drunk and
steal anyone's organs, like our old robot.

00:13:12.016 --> 00:13:13.017
Bender?

00:13:16.854 --> 00:13:18.898
Bender, it's me, Fry!

00:13:19.357 --> 00:13:20.441
Hyah!

00:13:32.912 --> 00:13:35.665
I knew Bender would turn up
purely by coincidence.

00:13:35.748 --> 00:13:38.167
Take care of him, but do it quietly.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:42.296
Don't worry. We're in space,
where no one can hear you clamp.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.383
What do you know?

00:13:45.466 --> 00:13:48.052
The Feds gave Bender a new identity
as a Moon farmer.

00:13:48.135 --> 00:13:49.971
He must be afraid to break character,

00:13:50.054 --> 00:13:52.723
in case there's any Robot Mafia
scuzzballs around.

00:13:52.807 --> 00:13:55.059
- Heh?
- Come on, let's go check on him.

00:13:56.519 --> 00:13:58.271
I checked on a guy once.

00:13:58.354 --> 00:14:00.564
I checked him into tiny pieces!

00:14:01.232 --> 00:14:04.944
Bender? Nope, don't recollect nobody
by that name.

00:14:05.027 --> 00:14:07.780
But let me ask my son-in-law. Billy?

00:14:07.947 --> 00:14:09.782
Yes, Moon-Pa?

00:14:09.865 --> 00:14:14.078
These nice big-city hillbillies are
looking for someone named Bender.

00:14:14.161 --> 00:14:15.162
You know him?

00:14:15.246 --> 00:14:18.582
Nope. He ain't any
of the eight people I ever met.

00:14:18.666 --> 00:14:20.334
Bender, it's us, your friends.

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:22.795
You can drop the hillbilly moron act.

00:14:22.878 --> 00:14:25.047
Sorry, mister, but I'm no Bender.

00:14:25.131 --> 00:14:27.008
I'm just a simple farmer.

00:14:27.091 --> 00:14:28.759
Name's Billy West.

00:14:28.843 --> 00:14:30.761
Billy West?

00:14:30.845 --> 00:14:33.014
What a stupid, phony, made-up name.

00:14:33.097 --> 00:14:37.685
You city folk are probably hungry
from premarital sex and flag-burning.

00:14:37.768 --> 00:14:39.520
Y'all wanna stay for supper?

00:14:39.604 --> 00:14:43.357
Well, my boyfriend and I were going
to have sex on a burning flag,

00:14:43.441 --> 00:14:45.026
but I could have a bite.

00:14:47.194 --> 00:14:51.741
May I present my beautiful robot wife,
the Crushinator.

00:14:51.824 --> 00:14:54.327
She's serving up the dinner and the charm.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:57.413
-Mashed chicken, Mr. Fry?
-Sure.

00:15:02.168 --> 00:15:04.754
So, uh, Billy, where were you born?

00:15:04.837 --> 00:15:06.881
Right here in Moon country.

00:15:06.964 --> 00:15:09.008
And how long have you been a farmer?

00:15:09.133 --> 00:15:11.385
Reckon I was born a farmer.

00:15:11.469 --> 00:15:13.721
Folks say my mama was a hoe.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:17.725
Oh, dear, I seem to have warped my fork.

00:15:17.808 --> 00:15:20.019
Could you bend it back for me, Billy?

00:15:20.645 --> 00:15:22.730
Bend it? I can't even lift it.

00:15:22.813 --> 00:15:26.817
Which is weird, seeing as how
my daddy was a forklift.

00:15:27.068 --> 00:15:31.238
Wow. Bender is really committed
to his new Jethrovian identity.

00:15:32.406 --> 00:15:36.869
If y'all are finished, I'll drive
y'all back to town in the old clunker.

00:15:39.121 --> 00:15:42.083
So, y'all flew here in a spacey ship?

00:15:42.166 --> 00:15:44.585
Stop talking like that!
You live on the Moon!

00:15:44.752 --> 00:15:48.047
If that is Bender, I guess he's just
happier in his new life.

00:15:48.255 --> 00:15:50.716
I refuse to believe anyone is happy!

00:15:50.925 --> 00:15:54.595
Mr. West, would you mind
if I examined your brain?

00:15:54.679 --> 00:15:58.432
Examine?
Heck, if you can find it, you can keep it.

00:16:04.055 --> 00:16:09.393
Gadzooks! Bender's hard drive no longer
contains any of his old memories!

00:16:09.477 --> 00:16:11.395
When the Feds bumpkinized him,

00:16:11.479 --> 00:16:14.190
they completely wiped out
his old identity!

00:16:15.358 --> 00:16:17.068
Well, I don't know about that,

00:16:17.151 --> 00:16:20.696
but who am I to argue
with a man from the sky?

00:16:20.988 --> 00:16:23.032
So long, space heroes.

00:16:27.578 --> 00:16:29.997
You sure you don't want
to kill all humans?

00:16:30.081 --> 00:16:32.458
I love all humans.

00:16:34.126 --> 00:16:35.795
He really is gone.

00:16:41.926 --> 00:16:43.386
I guess I'm happy for him.

00:16:43.469 --> 00:16:47.431
And honestly, Francis is a way
better friend than Bender ever was.

00:16:47.682 --> 00:16:49.475
Hey, where is Francis?

00:16:55.106 --> 00:16:58.067
One sarsapar-oil-la, Sheriff. I'm thirsty.

00:16:58.276 --> 00:17:00.778
Make it two. I'm greedy.

00:17:01.195 --> 00:17:04.240
You got the rest fooled, but not me.

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:08.119
Now let's take this outside,
so's no one else gets clamped.

00:17:08.202 --> 00:17:10.329
You're the boss, stranger.

00:17:13.833 --> 00:17:17.003
I'm gonna clamp your body parts off
one by one.

00:17:17.086 --> 00:17:20.506
But then I'm gonna clamp your wounds
shut so you stay alive

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:22.300
while I clamp you some more!

00:17:22.383 --> 00:17:24.343
Say your prayers, stoolie.

00:17:24.594 --> 00:17:28.014
Okay. God bless Grandma and Grandpa...

00:17:28.097 --> 00:17:31.726
They're next! Right now,
I'm gonna cut your damn head off!

00:17:34.979 --> 00:17:36.647
Drop the robot!

00:17:38.357 --> 00:17:42.695
I thought I told you,
I do the cutting around here.

00:18:07.136 --> 00:18:08.554
Scuttle on home.

00:18:08.638 --> 00:18:10.723
This ain't none of your business, slick.

00:18:10.973 --> 00:18:14.685
My name isn't Slick. It's Zoidberg.

00:18:14.977 --> 00:18:17.271
John -ing Zoidberg!

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:22.109
Stop! Zoidberg, you'll hurt Francis!

00:18:24.195 --> 00:18:26.489
Oh, yeah? Take this and that!

00:18:26.572 --> 00:18:28.366
Why, you lousy...

00:18:40.586 --> 00:18:42.380
I'm gonna clamp your...

00:18:42.463 --> 00:18:44.048
Oh, yeah.

00:18:44.173 --> 00:18:46.842
Ow, ow, ow.

00:18:46.926 --> 00:18:49.845
Looks like an all-you-can-kill
lobster fest!

00:18:50.263 --> 00:18:53.933
That offer was for a limited time only.

00:18:58.813 --> 00:19:00.523
My clamps!

00:19:00.773 --> 00:19:02.525
Why, Zoidberg, why?

00:19:02.608 --> 00:19:07.572
Because our friend Francis here,
is in reality a bad murderer.

00:19:07.655 --> 00:19:13.286
Yup. He was fixin' to kill me.
This here crawdad done saved my life!

00:19:16.372 --> 00:19:18.708
Bender, you two-timing jerk!

00:19:18.791 --> 00:19:21.168
I put off my singing career for you!

00:19:21.252 --> 00:19:23.838
If I can't have you, no one can!

00:19:26.257 --> 00:19:28.301
Oh, shucks.

00:19:29.927 --> 00:19:31.304
Bender! No!

00:19:31.387 --> 00:19:33.014
What?

00:19:40.229 --> 00:19:42.023
Bender was a hell of a squealer.

00:19:42.106 --> 00:19:43.983
Maybe the best there ever was.

00:19:44.275 --> 00:19:46.360
We'll send his widow some meatballs.

00:19:46.444 --> 00:19:48.946
Clamps, Bella, get in the way-back.

00:20:06.881 --> 00:20:08.132
To my friend, Bender.

00:20:08.299 --> 00:20:11.135
A wise man once said
he was a hell of a squealer.

00:20:11.302 --> 00:20:13.221
Maybe the best there ever was.

00:20:13.387 --> 00:20:14.722
To Bender!

00:20:16.224 --> 00:20:18.142
You pizza's gonna be another minute.

00:20:18.226 --> 00:20:20.728
We still waiting for it to be delivered.

00:20:20.811 --> 00:20:21.854
Bender?

00:20:21.938 --> 00:20:25.733
I'm no Bender.
You got me mixed up with another robot.

00:20:26.067 --> 00:20:27.902
You're probably right.

00:20:27.985 --> 00:20:30.154
I don't really remember
what he looks like.

00:20:30.363 --> 00:20:32.448
Guys, guys, it's me, Bender.

00:20:33.616 --> 00:20:34.659
He's alive!

00:20:34.867 --> 00:20:38.871
So that Moon hillbilly who got murdered
was just an innocent husband and father.

00:20:41.874 --> 00:20:45.002
Bender, old 'bot,
the Mafia thinks you're dead.

00:20:45.086 --> 00:20:47.255
You can come back to work with us.

00:20:47.338 --> 00:20:48.839
I'm back, baby!

00:20:48.923 --> 00:20:50.049
Pizza's here.

00:20:50.132 --> 00:20:51.175
Whoo!

00:20:51.259 --> 00:20:52.885
I'll just cut that...

00:20:53.511 --> 00:20:56.055
You do, and I'll -ing
gut you like a fish.